#: ../../../install.md:41
msgid "Option 1: Installation on Ubuntu Bionic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:43
msgid ""
"All of the Blueprint binaries are hosted in the osrfoundation repository. To "
"install all of them, the metapackage `ignition-blueprint` can be installed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:46
msgid ""
"sudo sh -c 'echo \"deb http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/ubuntu-"
"stable `lsb_release -cs` main\" > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/gazebo-stable."
"list'\n"
"wget http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo.key -O - | sudo apt-key add -\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install ignition-blueprint\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:53 ../../../install.md:72
msgid ""
"All libraries should be ready to use and the `ign gazebo` app ready to be "
"executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:55
msgid "Option 2: Install on MacOS Mojave (10.14)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:57
msgid ""
"All the Blueprint binaries are available in Mojave using the [homebrew "
"package manager](https://brew.sh/). The homebrew tool can easily be "
"installed using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:60
msgid ""
"/bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/"
"install/master/install.sh)\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:64
msgid ""
"After installing the homebrew package manager, Ignition Blueprint can be "
"installed running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:66
msgid ""
"brew tap osrf/simulation\n"
"brew trust osrf/simulation\n"
"brew install ignition-blueprint\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:74
msgid "Option 3: Source Installation (any platform)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:76
msgid ""
"The use of some additional tools is recommended to help with the source "
"compilation, although other ways of correctly getting and building the "
"sources are also possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:78
msgid ""
"Colcon supports python 3.5 (or higher) which is not the default option in "
"some platforms (like Ubuntu Bionic). The python [virtualenv](https://"
"virtualenv.pypa.io/en/latest/) could be a useful solution in cases where the "
"default option can not be easily changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:81
msgid "Installing vcstool and colcon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:83
msgid ""
"For getting the sources of all libraries the easiest way is to use [vcstool]"
"(https://github.com/dirk-thomas/vcstool). The tool is available from pip in "
"all platforms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:87
msgid "pip install vcstool\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:91
msgid ""
"Since Ignition libraries use `git` for version control it must be available "
"in the system for `vcstool` to work properly. In Ubuntu:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:93
msgid "sudo apt-get install git\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:97
msgid ""
"To compile all the different libraries and ign-gazebo in the right order it "
"is recommended to use [colcon](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/). "
"The colcon tool is available in all platforms using pip (or pip3, if pip "
"fails):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:101
msgid "pip install -U colcon-common-extensions\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:105
msgid "Use .deb packages in Ubuntu to install vcstool and colcon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:107
msgid ""
"An alternative method is to use the .deb packages available on Debian or "
"Ubuntu:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:109
msgid ""
"sudo sh -c 'echo \"deb http://packages.ros.org/ros/ubuntu $(lsb_release -sc) "
"main\" > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ros-latest.list'\n"
"\n"
"sudo apt-get install curl # if curl isn't already installed\n"
"curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros/rosdistro/master/ros.asc | "
"sudo apt-key add -\n"
"\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install python3-vcstool python3-colcon-common-extensions git\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:119
msgid "Getting the sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:121
msgid ""
"The instructions below use some UNIX commands to manage directories but the "
"obvious alternatives on Windows should provide the same result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:124
msgid ""
"The first step would be to create a developer workspace in which `vcstool` "
"and `colcon` can work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:127
msgid ""
"mkdir -p ~/workspace/src\n"
"cd ~/workspace/src\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:132
msgid ""
"All the sources of ignition-blueprint are declared in a yaml file. Download "
"it to the workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:135
msgid ""
"wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ignition-tooling/gazebodistro/master/"
"collection-blueprint.yaml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:139
msgid ""
"Use `vcstool` to automatically retrieve all the Ignition libraries sources "
"from their repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:142
msgid "vcs import < collection-blueprint.yaml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:146
msgid "The src subdirectory should contain all the sources ready to be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:148
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:150
msgid ""
"Before compiling it is necessary to install all the dependencies of the "
"different packages that compose the Blueprint collection. Every platform has "
"a different method to install software dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:154
msgid "Add packages.osrfoundation.org to the apt sources list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:156
msgid ""
"sudo sh -c 'echo \"deb http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/ubuntu-"
"stable `lsb_release -cs` main\" > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/gazebo-stable."
"list'\n"
"wget http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo.key -O - | sudo apt-key add -\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:162
msgid ""
"As reference the command below will install all dependencies in Ubuntu "
"Bionic:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:165
msgid ""
"sudo apt-get install cmake freeglut3-dev libavcodec-dev libavdevice-dev "
"libavformat-dev libavutil-dev libdart6-collision-ode-dev libdart6-dev "
"libdart6-utils-urdf-dev libfreeimage-dev libgflags-dev libglew-dev libgts-"
"dev libogre-1.9-dev libogre-2.1-dev libprotobuf-dev libprotobuf-dev "
"libprotoc-dev libqt5core5a libswscale-dev libtinyxml2-dev libtinyxml-dev pkg-"
"config protobuf-compiler python qml-module-qt-labs-folderlistmodel qml-"
"module-qt-labs-settings qml-module-qtquick2 qml-module-qtquick-controls qml-"
"module-qtquick-controls2 qml-module-qtquick-dialogs qml-module-qtquick-"
"layouts qml-module-qtqml-models2 qtbase5-dev qtdeclarative5-dev "
"qtquickcontrols2-5-dev ruby ruby-ronn uuid-dev libzip-dev libjsoncpp-dev "
"libcurl4-openssl-dev libyaml-dev libzmq3-dev libsqlite3-dev libwebsockets-"
"dev swig ruby-dev -y\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:169
msgid "Building the Ignition Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:171
msgid ""
"The Ignition Libraries require the following compilers on each platform:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:173
msgid "Ubuntu Bionic: gcc 8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:174
msgid "MacOS Mojave: Xcode 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:175
msgid "Windows: Visual Studio 2017"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:177
msgid "Installing gcc version 8 on Ubuntu Bionic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:179
msgid "To install `gcc` version 8 on Ubuntu Bionic:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:181
msgid "sudo apt-get install g++-8\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:185
msgid "Set `gcc-8` and `g++-8` to be the default compilers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:187
msgid ""
"sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/gcc gcc /usr/bin/gcc-8 800 --"
"slave /usr/bin/g++ g++ /usr/bin/g++-8 --slave /usr/bin/gcov gcov /usr/bin/"
"gcov-8\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:191
msgid ""
"At this point `gcc`  and `g++` should both report version 8. Test this with "
"the following commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:194
msgid ""
"gcc -v\n"
"g++ -v\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:199
msgid "Building the colcon workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:201
msgid ""
"Once the compiler and all the sources are in place it is time to compile "
"them. Start the procedure by changing into the workspace and listing the "
"packages recognized by `colcon`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:205
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace/\n"
"colcon list -g\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:210
msgid ""
"`colcon` should list the Ignition libraries with their interdependencies. If "
"that is the case, then you are ready to build the whole set of libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:214
msgid "colcon build --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:218
msgid "If there are no errors, all the binaries should be ready to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:220
msgid "Using the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:222
msgid ""
"The workspace binaries are ready but every time that `ign gazebo` needs to "
"be executed or third party code is going to be developed using the Ignition "
"libraries, one command is needed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:226
msgid ""
". ~/workspace/install/local_setup.bash\n"
"(or call ~/workspace/install/local_setup.bat on Windows)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:231
msgid ""
"After running the command all paths for running apps or developing code will "
"be set in the current shell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:234
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:236
msgid "Unable to create the rendering window"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:238
msgid ""
"If you're getting errors like \"Unable to create the rendering window\", it "
"could mean you're using an old OpenGL version. Gazebo Sim uses the Ogre 2 "
"rendering engine by default, which requires an OpenGL version higher than "
"3.3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:242
msgid ""
"This can be confirmed by checking the Ogre 2 logs at `~/.ignition/rendering/"
"ogre2.log`, which should have an error like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:245
msgid ""
"\"OGRE EXCEPTION(3:RenderingAPIException): OpenGL 3.3 is not supported. "
"Please update your graphics card drivers.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:247
msgid "You can also check your OpenGL version running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:249
msgid "glxinfo | grep \"OpenGL version\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:251
msgid ""
"You should be able to use Ogre 1 without any issues however. You can check "
"if that's working by running a world which uses Ogre 1 instead of Ogre 2, "
"such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:254
msgid "ign gazebo -v 3 lights.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:256
msgid ""
"If that loads, you can continue to use Ignition with Ogre 1, just be sure to "
"specify `ogre` in your SDF files instead of `ogre2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:259
msgid ""
"To enable Ogre 2 support, you'll need to update your computer's OpenGL "
"version. As suggested on the Ogre logs, this may require updating your "
"graphics card drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:263
msgid ""
"The Ogre 2 debs from the osrfoundation repository are built from a fork of "
"Ogre's `v2-1` branch with changes needed for deb packaging and allowing it "
"to be co-installable with Ogre 1.x. The code can be found here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.md:267
msgid "https://github.com/osrf/ogre-2.1-release"
msgstr ""
